WEBVTT

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:25.420
T'would seem all the pieces on the game
board are moving just as you wish them to.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.590
I'm just getting started.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.510
Rika needs to suffer far more.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.310
She thought she had escaped
her hundred years of torture,

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:42.900
only to be dragged back
into the cycle of tragedy...

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:48.820
Each loop is a sharp burr,
digging into the cat's mind...

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.650
I'm quite grateful for this power.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.110
With your gracious gift,

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:56.660
I'm now able to force
my stubborn Rika into capitulating.

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:00.710
No thanks are necessary.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:07.880
Your antics allow me to stave off
my most detested state: boredom.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.300
While I don't understand what
you find so entertaining about me,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.300
I'm glad you enjoy it so.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.640
Now, child...

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.430
...do not forget this most
important of facts.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.190
You have rolled the dice
and begun the game.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:29.530
You can no longer withdraw.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:35.030
As long as your death
occurs after the cat's,

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:38.330
you will always travel
to the same fragment.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:39.490
However...

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:44.670
If your death comes to pass
while the cat is still alive,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:48.040
you will be transported to a fragment
where the cat does not exist:

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.760
one where she was never even born.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.970
You do not object to these conditions?

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:58.890
I would hardly make
such a careless mistake.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.900
Of course you wouldn't.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:15.860
Too close.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.700
I-I'm sorry!

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.540
You're not "au-au"-ing for me this time.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.830
Huh?

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.750
Never mind.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:29.420
Since I've got you here, let's have
ourselves a constructive discussion.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.630
Though if I'm here,
it means a tragedy occurred again.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:37.220
You can take a little break
if you're still in pain.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.180
You shouldn't force yourself.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.350
Sure.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:44.940
If you're promising me that a tragedy
won't occur in the next world,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.480
then I'll shut up and lie here
with my eyes closed.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.570
Or are you going to rescue me?

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:56.070
What'll it be, Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>?

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.570
I'm sorry.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:03.750
What should I do?
What should I have done?!

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:08.170
I told Keiichi to give the doll to Mion,

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:11.800
but it didn't work! Nothing changed!

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:17.470
Shion and Keiichi snuck into the ritual
toolshed and Kimiyoshi went missing!

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.100
Rika, the person who killed you--

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.930
--was probably Shion.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:27.560
If <i>someone's </i>power wasn't so lacking,
maybe I could actually remember who!

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.150
Please, calm down and think it over.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:36.530
Go over the things you <i>can </i>remember.
You might find some hints!

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.410
I don't want to.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.530
Rika...

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.370
I don't want anyone to die.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:47.160
I don't want my friends
or the villagers to die anymore.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.290
I'm sorry.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:55.010
I don't want to die anymore.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.180
Rika?!

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:18.860
Whatever is the matter?!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.820
N-Nothing!

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.330
I was just remembering
a really scary dream.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.290
I'm okay.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.340
You don't look "okay" at all.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.520
Satoko! Satoko!

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.110
Why is this happening?!
Why do I have to keep doing this?!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.490
If your nightmare was that horrible,

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:08.080
maybe it's not merely a dream, but a sign.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.290
A sign?

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.710
What do you mean, a sign? From who?

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:19.130
Well, I'd assume it was
from a divine being.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.880
Like...

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.010
Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>!

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:33.060
Oyashiro-<i>sama </i>is the divine protector
of Hinamizawa, after all.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:39.280
Oyashiro-<i>sama </i>must be trying to tell you
something through your nightmares.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.610
What is he trying to tell me...

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.490
...by putting me through all this?

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.240
I couldn't tell you.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.910
But Oyashiro-<i>sama </i>isn't an evil god.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:56.000
He just wants you to be happy.
That's what he's trying to tell you.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.130
But he isn't telling me anything!
There's no hidden message!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:05.800
No matter what I do, the nightmares
never end! They just keep going!

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.140
Hey, Rika?

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:12.640
I swear I won't tell anyone,
so please, answer honestly.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:18.610
Have you done anything
to make Oyashiro-<i>sama </i>mad,

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.030
or even <i>thought </i>about it?

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.360
Does anything ring a bell?

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.660
No, I haven't.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.290
I'm a good priestess!

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.590
You liar.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.430
Did you say something?

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:52.520
I heard you talking in your sleep once.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.560
Huh?

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.190
"I hate living in the hick village
of Hinamizawa.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:02.730
I want to leave here and
go to Fancy Name Academy instead."

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:10.660
One of Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s rules is
you can never leave the village, right?

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:13.580
And you're a priestess
at the Furude Shrine, Rika.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:16.500
Th-That was a long time ago!

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:20.380
We can go on trips now!
We go to Okinomiya all the time to shop!

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:23.380
I promise I won't tell anyone.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:28.300
Tell me, do you really want
something so blasphemous?

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.810
Th-There's nothing wrong with
wanting to go to a certain school!

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.980
Even I have the right to dream!

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:42.820
But you're Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s priestess.
Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s reincarnation, right?

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.740
I don't care about that!

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:49.160
I was born into that role!
I didn't get a choice!

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.870
I didn't want any of this!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.590
So, Rika.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.050
Why do you want to leave Hinamizawa?

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.940
Look how beautiful it is here.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.320
Look how nice the weather is today.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:32.070
The village always cared for us.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.950
We played in its rivers,
walked between its fields,

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.040
looked down upon it
from the mountaintops...

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:44.840
Every single moment of our lives,
Hinamizawa was watching over us.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:49.340
But then you said
you hated this "hick village."

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.590
If I were Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>,

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:56.560
I'd probably think
you were a little ungrateful.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:09.110
If these nightmares you're having
are his way of punishing you...

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.860
If he's punishing me?

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:13.740
...maybe you should clear your mind...

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:18.250
...and think of all the wonderful things
here in Hinamizawa

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:21.290
that you've just happened to forget about.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.790
I'm sure if you do...

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.550
...you won't have any more nightmares.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.720
I'm sorry.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:43.810
You've had bad times in this village, too,
but I was only thinking about myself.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:45.360
It's okay.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:50.690
I'm just happy getting
to be here with you, Rika.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.320
Satoko...

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.660
Thank you.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.040
Saturday, June 11th, 1983

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.050
Okinomiya
 Titans

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.050
Hinamizawa 
Fighters

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:17.100
We're still in this! It's only two outs!

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:19.560
This is our last chance.

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:26.400
We were stomping them until
that pitcher got on the mound...

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:31.110
You're so cool, Mii! You hit home runs
to both left and right field!

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:34.910
Your bat actually connects
with the ball, unlike Satoko!

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:38.580
Rika! You'll pay for that comment later!

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:44.250
Hey, that's good!

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:44.250
Go, go, go!

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:45.620
Safe!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.130
Hell yeah!

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:48.960
Satoko-<i>chan</i>'s up next!

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.960
All right...

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.880
Say goodbye to the ball,
because I'm going to hit a home run!

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.680
How's Satoko done in her last at bats?

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:01.180
Um, she struck out every time.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.850
Her bat was <i>this </i>far away from the ball!

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.270
Huh. I see what she's doing.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:11.230
Keiichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.740
Satoko-<i>chan</i>, Keiichi-<i>kun</i>'s here!

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.150
Keiichi-<i>kun</i>'s here to help us!

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:25.080
What is Keiichi-<i>kun </i>doing?

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:37.380
Yes!

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.550
What?!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.140
I don't even need to run the bases!

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.930
We won, Keiichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.520
Why did you even need me?

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:51.860
Dammit!

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:53.570
A perfectly placed trap!

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:58.410
Just play it cool until the very
last moment to ensnare your opponent!

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:01.910
All right, Coach,
you remember the deal, right?

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.740
Monday, June 12th, 1983

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.330
Wow, you guys are early!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.210
My, <i>there </i>you are.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:18.220
If only you'd arrived later.
Then I could have eaten all of your meat!

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.800
Think again, Satoko!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:25.270
I'll use my superior reach to snatch
the best bits away from you!

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:29.230
E-Excuse me?! I-I absolutely
will <i>not </i>let you get away with that!

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:33.650
Calm down, I'll let you have
some bell peppers and eggplant.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:38.360
I'll let you have lots and lots
of roast squash!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.910
Squash?!

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:44.660
I'll let Coach know how much
you looove squash, Satoko.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:49.410
I'm sure Coach would go out and
buy you all the squash in the country!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:54.630
Ain't that something, Satoko! You'll have
squash for breakfast, lunch, and dinner!

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.920
Rena-<i>san</i>!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.760
W-Wait! Don't go to her, or she'll--

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:09.640
Stop that, Keiichi-<i>kun</i>! She's mine!
And I'm taking her home!

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:15.650
Don't just stand there!
Mion-<i>san</i>, Rika, you get in on it, too!

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:35.710
--I'm gonna take these ones.
--Man, that was so good...

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.500
Might I ask for a favor?

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.220
Rika-<i>chan</i>? Wait, where's Satoko?

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:46.600
Satoko went to go shopping for dinner.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:49.600
She did? At just the right time, too.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:52.270
She totally skipped out on clean-up!

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:56.360
Unlike you, Keiichi,
Satoko is really clever!

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:17.210
Oh yeah, here we go,
that's what I'm talking about!

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.340
<i>Ron!</i>

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:22.550
Man, I blew it! Wait, I'm still in this...

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:26.180
I believe I have myself a double <i>ron </i>here.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.350
What?

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.680
<i>Yakuman?!</i>

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.400
Damn, you and Satoko-<i>chan</i>
wiped the floor with us today!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:40.190
Talk about a one-two punch.
You guys win this one!

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:43.530
Hell yeah, Satoko! We won!

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:46.320
Oh, sorry.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:48.740
Satoko!

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.750
Man, Satoko-<i>chan</i>'s gotten damn good!

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.410
Bet she could be
a pro player in the future!

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:57.080
That's my niece for ya!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:01.420
Smart <i>and </i>cute!
She'll beat anyone at <i>any </i>game!

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.340
All right, let's do another!

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:07.680
Sorry, but that's gonna be our last.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:11.930
What? But it's so early.
The sun ain't even set yet.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:15.560
I gotta walk Satoko back before dark.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.480
If somethin' happened to her
walking back at night,

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:19.940
I'd never be able to live with myself!

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.320
You sure have changed, Tecchan.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.490
They say nothin' changes
a man like a woman.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:31.700
Who knew she'd be this little, though?

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:36.540
Satoko's the only family I got left.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:41.040
I ain't the same man I was before.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:45.220
Now, I'd die for Satoko if I had to.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:51.050
You're so damn cool.
I'll be real, I like this new Tecchan!

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.640
Thanks for coming by to hang out.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:02.020
If I didn't, your apartment
would turn into a landfill again.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:05.610
Then all my hard work
cleaning it would be put to waste.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:11.320
Thanks. I've never had to take care of
my own place before, so, y'know.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.130
I expected worse from you, Uncle.

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:24.340
Here I thought you
would have spent this all.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:29.630
I only take out what I need to get by.
I ain't gonna waste a penny.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:34.470
Just thought, if something
were to happen to me,

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:37.140
I'd want there to be some left for you.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.230
May I ask you something, Uncle?

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:46.610
Would you <i>really </i>die for me?

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:49.610
Yeah, of course I would!

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:54.620
If you ever need somethin' from me,
I'll throw my whole life into it!

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:01.880
Uncle, will you come
live with me in Hinamizawa?

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:02.830
Huh?

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:06.420
I need your help with something, Uncle.

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:16.430
She's been out shopping for far too long.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:26.320
Could you tell me what it is
you need help with now?

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:27.690
Well...

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:40.910
I know you haven't lived here for a while.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:45.340
Do you not want anyone to know we're here?

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.850
The hell are you lookin' at?!

00:17:57.850 --> 00:17:59.350
N-Nothing!

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:04.310
C'mon, get inside, Satoko.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:06.610
Yes, Uncle Teppei.

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:25.790
Thank you for that.
I didn't want them to stare at me.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:28.250
You'll be safe in here.

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:31.380
Nobody can hear ya, either.

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:34.840
Oh, Uncle...

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:42.060
The truth is, I'm being
horribly bullied here.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:48.230
By who? Who's the bastard
who's bullying you?!

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:53.190
I'll punch their lights out!

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:54.150
Don't.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.860
Why the hell not?!

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:59.200
Just tell me who's doin' it
and I'll take care of them!

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.540
It's not just one person.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.620
It's everyone in Hinamizawa.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.170
<i>Everyone?</i>

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:11.210
That's why punching one or
two people won't fix anything,

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.720
it'll just make things worse.

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:17.970
Why are they doin' this to you?

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:19.550
You know why.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:24.890
It's because my parents were
the leaders of the pro-dam movement.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.140
What?

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:32.780
But my brother was the one who did
all that! You had nothin' to do with it!

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:36.450
The village considers
the Hojo family their enemy.

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:39.990
And the village comes together
to fight off their enemies.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:42.620
That's how Hinamizawa works.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:53.590
I just want to get along with everyone
and live here with a smile.

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:57.260
That's all I want,
just one little thing...

00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:59.760
But apparently Satoko Hojo is...

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:04.560
...a bad person you should throw rocks at!

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:11.820
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry, Satoko!

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:15.070
I had no idea this was happenin' to you!

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:20.120
Please forgive me for bein'
so goddamn shameful! I'm sorry!

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:26.500
It's okay. It's not your fault, Uncle.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.000
But if you wouldn't mind,

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.000
could you live here
with me for a little while?

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:32.580
Huh?

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:35.010
I'm so tired.

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:37.630
If I can't be happy out there,

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.880
at least I can be happy
at home with my family.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.430
Sa... Satoko!

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:53.190
So you will plunge yourself into
a delightful pool of pity, then?

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.030
Teppei Hojo is here?

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:59.610
Yeah, someone saw him outside their house.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:04.490
That horribly violent man?
What is he doing back here <i>now</i>?

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:09.580
Bet he did somethin' in Okinomiya and
had to get outta town. This ain't good.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:14.540
We gotta tell the mayor.
Maybe Oryo-<i>san </i>can do somethin'.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:18.090
I just feel bad
for Satoko-<i>chan</i>, the poor girl...

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:43.530
Satoko!

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:49.330
I was so worried.
Let's get dinner started!

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.040
Rika.

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:54.040
I came to get my things.

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:55.630
Huh?

00:21:55.630 --> 00:21:59.210
I'm going to be living with
my uncle from now on.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:08.430
How distraught the cat must feel!

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:14.270
My goodness, the two of you
are so <i>very </i>entertaining!

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
Tatariakashi-hen:
Curse-Revealing Chapter, Part 2

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:49.910
Next time: "Tatariakashi-hen:
Curse-Revealing Chapter, Part 2."
